// THE FLOAT-USING HALF OF `opcode_witness.kel`, SPLIT OUT SO ITS REFUSAL DOES
// NOT COST EVERY OTHER OPCODE ITS WITNESS.
//
// This file exists because of a measured regression, not a preference. When the
// native backend's float guard was widened to catch a float CONSTANT -- a route
// that previously escaped it, because the guard scanned signatures only -- the
// whole of `opcode_witness.kel` became refused at MODULE level. It carries
// `let scaled = f + 1.5;`, so one float constant took `BoundsCheck`,
// `CheckedDiv`, `CheckedMod` and `CallExternalNative` out of the lowering
// census with it, even though none of them has anything to do with floats.
//
// THE FIX BELONGS IN THE CORPUS, NOT IN THE GUARD. Weakening a correct refusal
// to recover coverage is the trade this line refuses on principle. Splitting the
// program is the alternative that costs nothing true.
//
// WHAT IT WITNESSES: `IntToFloat` and `FloatToInt`, which the backend refuses
// and will keep refusing until the float representation is decided -- the entry
// application binary interface is `i64` where a double belongs, so there is a
// live defect and not merely a missing feature. This file is EXPECTED to sit in
// the differential's exempt set as a backend refusal.
//
// Divisors and operands are constants so no argument vector can make it fault.
//
// WITNESSES: IntToFloat, FloatToInt
//
// THE LINE ABOVE IS A MACHINE-CHECKED CLAIM, not a comment.
// `witness_integrity.rs` compiles this file and asserts every opcode named
// there is actually emitted. A witness that silently STOPS witnessing --
// because the reference compiler folded the construct away, or because a
// function moved to another file -- would otherwise drop a census figure
// with nothing going red.
//
// That is not hypothetical: the `Op::IsStruct` construct was repaired out of
// existence by the `v0.2.3` line one hour after this corpus adopted it.

fn float_round_trip(w: Word) -> Word {
  let f = w as Float;
  let scaled = f + 1.5;
  scaled as Word
}

fn main(seed: Word) -> Word {
  float_round_trip(seed)
}
